  "8fc79b6d-2372-4f9d-80cf-9b2785d17a70": {
   "id": "8fc79b6d-2372-4f9d-80cf-9b2785d17a70",
   "message": {
    "id": "8fc79b6d-2372-4f9d-80cf-9b2785d17a70",
    "author": {
     "role": "assistant",
     "name": null,
     "metadata": {}
    },
    "create_time": 1774583021.705,
    "update_time": null,
    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport krippendorff  # pip install krippendorff\n\ndf = pd.read_csv(\"triple_labels.csv\")  # window_id, rater, label\n# reliability matrix: raters x units\nmat = df.pivot(index=\"rater\", columns=\"window_id\", values=\"label\")\n\n# map string labels to ints, keep NaN for missing\ncodes = {lab: i for i, lab in enumerate(sorted(df[\"label\"].unique()))}\nmat = mat.apply(lambda col: col.map(codes))\n\nalpha = krippendorff.alpha(reliability_data=mat.to_numpy(dtype=float),\n                           level_of_measurement=\"nominal\")\nprint(f\"Krippendorff's alpha (nominal): {alpha:.3f}\")\n```\n\nSanity checks before you trust the number:\n- `mat.shape` should be `(3, 412)`.\n- `mat.isna().sum().sum()` should be 0 if every window was triple labeled.\n- Print `df.groupby(\"rater\").label.value_counts(normalize=True)`. If one rater uses \"stalled\" much more often than the others, that will drag alpha down more than kappa."
     ]
    },
